# lib/ecs — hierarchy components (docs/ecs-general-architecture.md §2.4).
#
# The parent/child relationship expressed as ECS components, defined ONCE here so
# ANY World (UI or game) can parameterise ComponentTable over them instead of
# each app redeclaring its own. `Children` on a parent is the AUTHORITATIVE,
# ordered child list; `Parent` is the cached upward pointer for traversal. The
# HierarchySystem (#711/#712) owns keeping them in sync and repairing them on
# destroy. Both are plain data — no methods.
import core
open ecs/entity

# The authoritative, ordered list of an entity's children (stored on the parent).
type Children {
  ids: List(EntityId)
}

# The cached upward pointer to an entity's parent — the reverse of Children,
# kept in sync by the HierarchySystem.
type Parent {
  parent: EntityId
}
